<%#
  Common settings — Window Focus (issue #992 split). A card on the settings
  window's General tab. Focus iRacing is a three-way mode since #977. Emits
  items only — the includer supplies the heading. Its Connection item
  (`disableWhenDisconnected`) was retired in #1599; the disconnected look is the
  Appearance tab's `global-disconnected-look.ejs`.
%>
<sdpi-item label="Focus iRacing">
  <sdpi-select setting="focusIRacingWindow" global default="always">
    <option value="always">Always</option>
    <option value="required">When required</option>
    <option value="never">Never</option>
  </sdpi-select>
</sdpi-item>
<div class="ird-supporting-text">
  Brings iRacing to the foreground so a press isn't lost to whichever window happens
  to be active. <strong>Always</strong> does it before every key press, dial press and
  dial turn. <strong>When required</strong> does it only before something that needs the
  foreground: a keyboard binding, a chat command, or a touch-strip gesture that taps a
  binding — keys that talk to iRacing over its API, SimHub roles and plugin-only keys
  leave your window alone. <strong>Never</strong> leaves focus alone entirely.
</div>
